database is running, it automatically scales between the min and max \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://neon.com/docs/introduction/autoscaling\",\"children\":\"autoscaling limits\"}],\" you set.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Your monthly compute usage will reflect what your application actually used, not some preallocated block.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"For databases that don’t run 24/7, Neon automatically scales to zero after a period of inactivity (5 minutes by default). You can \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://neon.com/docs/guides/scale-to-zero-guide\",\"children\":\"configure this behavior\"}],\", but it makes Neon incredibly efficient for dev/test databases or projects that have quiet periods (e.g. outside of business hours).\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n66:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"The metric we use to bill compute is CU-hour:\"}]\n67:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"A CU (Compute Unit) is a measure of your compute size: 1 CU = 1 vCPU + 4 GB RAM\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"A CU-hour represents 1 CU running for 1 hour\"}],\"\\n\"]}]\n68:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Example:\"}],\" If a 2 CU database runs for 3 hours, that’s 6 CU-hours. Our billing engine keeps track of this automatically, summing up all your real usage across all databases at the end of the month.\"]}]\n69:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"storage-usage-gb-months\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Storage usage (GB-months)\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#storage-usage-gb-months\",\"